{"name":"Białowieża Forest","hex":"#1c5022","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"forest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dense uncultivated tract of trees and undergrowth, larger than woods.","Any dense collection or amount."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover an area with trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Białowieża Forest","blocks":[{"text":"Białowieża Forest is a large forest complex and World Heritage Area straddling the border between Poland and Belarus. It is one of the last and the largest remaining parts of the immense primeval forest that once stretched across the European Plain. The forest is home to more than 800 European bison, Europe's heaviest land animal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Bialowieza_National_Park_in_Poland0029.JPG/330px-Bialowieza_National_Park_in_Poland0029.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bia%C5%82owie%C5%BCa_Forest","wikidata":"Q192666"},{"title":"Białowieża","blocks":[{"text":"Białowieża is a village in Poland's Podlaskie Voivodeship, in the middle of the Białowieża Forest, to which it gave its name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Bialowieza_beentree.jpg/330px-Bialowieza_beentree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bia%C5%82owie%C5%BCa","wikidata":"Q2334100"},{"title":"Forest","blocks":[{"text":"A forest is an ecosystem characterized by a dense community of trees. Hundreds of definitions of forest are used throughout the world, incorporating factors such as tree density, tree height, land use, legal standing, and ecological function. The United Nations' Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) defines a forest as, \"Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban use.\" Using this definition, Global Forest Resources Assessment 2025 found that forests covered 4.14 billion hectares, or approximately 31 percent of the world's land area in 2025."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg/330px-Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest","wikidata":"Q4421"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Puszcza_Bia%C5%82owieska_-_orientacyjne_po%C5%82o%C5%BCenie.png/500px-Puszcza_Bia%C5%82owieska_-_orientacyjne_po%C5%82o%C5%BCenie.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Puszcza_Bia%C5%82owieska_-_orientacyjne_po%C5%82o%C5%BCenie.png/500px-Puszcza_Bia%C5%82owieska_-_orientacyjne_po%C5%82o%C5%BCenie.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Approximate range of the Białowieża Primeval Forest in Poland and Belarus.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APuszcza_Bia%C5%82owieska_-_orientacyjne_po%C5%82o%C5%BCenie.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Belovezhskaya_Puscha_coat_of_arms_on_envelope_of_the_Belarus_2009.png/500px-Belovezhskaya_Puscha_coat_of_arms_on_envelope_of_the_Belarus_2009.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Belovezhskaya_Puscha_coat_of_arms_on_envelope_of_the_Belarus_2009.png/500px-Belovezhskaya_Puscha_coat_of_arms_on_envelope_of_the_Belarus_2009.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Belovezhskaya Pushcha coat of arms on Pre-Stamped Envelope of the